            "Sea ice is bright: it reflects 50% to 70% of the sunlight, while the dark sea reflects less than 10%. Less ice means more heat absorbed and further melting: the **ice–albedo feedback**. That is one of the reasons the Arctic is warming about four times as fast as the planet as a whole.",
